    "q-162764": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162764",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Use the method of Lagrange multipliers to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+1\\,$ on the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "We must find the minimum value of $f(x,y)$ subject to the constraint $g(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ \n\nSince $f(x,y)$ is continuous and the constraint is closed and bounded, $f(x,y)$ reaches a global maximum and a global minimum on the constraint. \n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y),\\,g(x,y)=4\n$$\n\nWe start by solving the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x}(x,y),{f}_{y}(x,y)⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x}(x,y),{g}_{y}(x,y)⟩ \\\\ ⟨4x,-2y⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,2y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4x=2\\lambda x \\\\ -2y=2\\lambda y\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x(2-\\lambda )=0 \\\\ y(\\lambda +1)=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we break it up into several cases:\n\n- Assuming $x=0$ in the first equation of the system, the constraint condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4 & =0\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,-2),(0,2).$\n\n- Assuming $\\lambda =2$ in the first equation of the system, the second equation of the system implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2+1)=0\\,⇒\\,y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the constraint condition ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0$ implies\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(2,0),(-2,0).$\n\nTherefore, $f$ has possible extreme values at the points\n\n$$\n(0,\\pm 2),\\,(\\pm 2,0).\n$$\n\nWe evaluate $f$ at these points. These are given in the following table:\n\n| $(x,y)$ | $(0,\\pm 2)$ | $(\\pm 2,0)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x,y)$ | $-3$ | $9$ |\n\nTherefore, the function reaches a minimum value at the points $(0,\\pm 2)$ and its minimum value is $-3.$",
